{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-21 permits a driver to reroute from the recommended route in response to real-time traffic or congestion, and that is exactly what this record shows. EV-ADVIS-06014-01 is an LTA advisory of type HEAVY_TRAFFIC for Central Expressway (CTE) towards AYE after the Outram Road exit, valid 17:43:57 to 18:55:37, which covers the trip window recorded in EV-TRIP-06014 (started 18:05:37, ended 18:28:37). The driver left the recommended route at the CTE / Outram Road exit at 18:14:48 and rejoined it at Alexandra Road / Henderson Road at 18:26:20 (EV-TRIP-06014), and EV-GPS-06014's trace shows the map-matched road changing from Central Expressway (CTE) to Outram Road between 18:14:07 and 18:14:37. The reroute was a direct response to reported congestion on the corridor the driver was travelling, not a detour for the driver's own purposes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06014-01", "EV-TRIP-06014", "EV-GPS-06014"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-06014-01.payload.derived.v7.overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Whether this reroute is traffic-justified within POL-RD-23 is left open by the evidence itself, and POL-RD-23 is the test that matters: the advisory must intersect the recommended route and overlap the trip window. EV-ADVIS-06014-01 returns intersects_route and justifies_reroute as null and states on its face that the record does not say whether the advisory lies on the recommended route (its 'undetermined' value is 'on the recommended route'). The window limb is satisfied; the intersection limb is not established by the artifact that carries it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06014-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-06014-01.payload.derived.v7.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the fact 'whether traffic justified the reroute' cannot be established on this record, POL-GEN-26 requires the case to be escalated rather than decided, and an escalated amount is held rather than refunded. Escalation preserves the driver's position for the human reviewer instead of confirming the interim clawback against him on evidence that does not settle the question.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06014-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-06014-01.payload.derived.v7.justifies_reroute",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-24 provides that exactly one row applies, and its rows divide on the traffic-justification limb: rows (a) to (c) require the reroute to be traffic-justified and rows (d) to (e) require it not to be. With that limb unresolved, no single row can be selected, so this is a case that fits no row, and POL-RD-24 directs that such a case is escalated under POL-GEN-26.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06014-01", "EV-TRIP-06014"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-06014-01.payload.derived.v7.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-25 allows a route-deviation ruling to stand only at a confidence of 0.80 or more and otherwise sends the case to escalation. With the advisory's intersection unresolved on the artifact that carries it, no monetary ruling on this reroute can be made at that confidence, so the ruling cannot stand and the case must go to a human reviewer with the 1.58 SGD held.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06014-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-06014-01.payload.derived.v7.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The most the route-deviation matrix can move on this trip is the excess distance fare, and it is 1.58 SGD and no more: POL-RD-24 fixes it as the deviation distance (1.50 km — EV-TRIP-06014's 11.4 km actual minus 9.9 km recommended) multiplied by fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd (1.05 SGD, EV-FARE-06014), without surge. That is precisely the sum already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver, so the driver contests only that 1.58 SGD and claims no part of the 28.94 SGD trip fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06014", "EV-FARE-06014"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-FARE-06014.payload.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not rest his case on the rider having been informed, and the record shows why that limb cannot carry the decision either way without review: no chat notice of the deviation appears in EV-CHAT-06014 — its two messages are both sent before the trip began (18:04:07 and 18:04:37) and both concern the pickup point — and EV-TRIP-06014 records no in-app call, so POL-RD-21's notice requirement is met neither by a chat message nor by a recorded verbal notice. The question this record genuinely leaves open is traffic justification, which is where the case must be sent for review.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06014", "EV-TRIP-06014"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-TRIP-06014.payload.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 1.58 SGD clawback was never a final determination: EV-TRIP-06014's fare_adjusted event records the sum as 'refunded to rider and recovered from driver earnings pending review', and EV-FARE-06014 shows the payment status as PARTIALLY_REFUNDED with 1.58 SGD refund_issued_sgd. POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION the confirmation of the present state, and the present state is expressly provisional; the disposition that fits a provisional adjustment is the review POL-RD-25 provides for, not its finalisation against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06014", "EV-FARE-06014"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-TRIP-06014.payload.events[].event_type",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
